 "comment": "WP-4.2 soak (PLAN_v4 section 5 Phase 4 row 4.2): two in-game days of a seed-8675309 generated world with no save (SaveHandlerMP). The player (id 0) works four sites in turn: (X, Z) = (-40, 24) from t=0, (-40, 524) from t=12000, (-640, 24) from t=24000, back to (-40, 24) at t=36000. A site is a 15 x 9 stone platform at y = 100 (x X-7..X+7, z Z-4..Z+4, the 15 x 12 x 9 box above it cleared to air first, so the site does not depend on the terrain and the scenario runs under check-sensitivity.sh's flipped seed), built with fill/set_block ops at the tick the player arrives: the player at (X-5.5, 101, Z+0.5); a dirt block beside it dug with the stone shovel (8 dig ticks from t+2, broken on the 4th; the drop is picked up), dirt placed back with use_item at t+20 and a torch at t+21; birch, spruce and oak saplings on dirt (random-tick growth, WorldGenForest / WorldGenTaiga2 / WorldGenTrees or BigTree); a farm row (two farmland blocks with crops around a still-water block, cactus on sand and reeds on dirt beside the water); two leaves blocks with the check-decay bit (no log in range: they decay on a random tick and may drop a sapling); sand and gravel in the air (falling-sand entities); a fenced 2 x 2 pen with a pig and a chicken (eggs); a cobblestone item out of the player's reach (despawns at age 6000); outside the platform, three one-block pillars: flowing water at (X+11, 101, Z) and flowing lava at (X, 101, Z-9) pouring down to the terrain (long fluid cascades, lava fires on the ground) and an eternal fire on netherrack at (X+11, 101, Z-4) next to a plank. Moving on, set_pos puts the player on the next site (y = feet + (double) 1.62F, the yOffset, since set_pos is Entity.setPosition) with set_motion 0; a revisited site is not rebuilt. Difficulty 0 with natural spawning on (the reproducible setting, tools/oracle/census.md section 3: animals and squid spawn, hostile spawning stays off). set_weather at t=0 sets thunder_time to 100000000 so no thunderstorm starts during the run: lightning bolts draw from a never-seeded Entity.rand (census section 3) and one striking near an entity would make the oracle irreproducible; rain_time 6000 starts the first rain at t=6000. Every op position is preloaded before tick 0 (5 x 5 chunks); the player then loads the 19 x 19 chunks around it (random ticks, World.updateBlocksAndPlayCaveSounds) and generates and populates them at each new site; nothing unloads (b1.7.3 has no chunk dropping in single player). Animals left behind more than 128 blocks despawn (EntityLiving.despawnEntity). Dumps (tests/golden/README.md \"Soak\"): rng_state every 100 ticks; the player's entity line every 500; world_time, weather, scheduled_ticks, player_state, inventory, every entity, and the chunk_digest of the 3 x 3 chunks around every site every 1000; at the last tick additionally the rest of each site's 5 x 5 chunks, a block_box over each site and the full scheduled-tick list.",
